dland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Yan Cantu","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Running casing good no issues, all time good comunication wite the hands the rig ","location":"HP267","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75922588","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Shon Rodgers","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Smart tool was leaking at the service loop causing the bails to bleed off before the crt was disengaged","location":"Cactus 404 / rig floor ","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75913016","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Raymundo Guevara","type":"Recognition","description":"job went good everyone was safe and did a great job looking agter on another","location":"patterson 289","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75912942","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Kayla Magana","type":"Recognition","description":"Field Evaluation\n\nEmployee: Pedro\nLocation: OXY - BRU 5304\nScope of Work: Reset Anchor\nPedro was observed performing anchor reset operations on the OXY BRU 5304 location.\nHe arrived on location prepared and compliant with all OXY and company requirements. Prior to beginning work, Pedro properly completed the OXY Ground Disturbance Permit book and Job Safety Analysis (JSA), demonstrating a clear understanding of site-specific hazards and mitigation procedures. Documentation was thorough, legible, and aligned with company safety standards.\nPedro exhibited strong working knowledge of his job description and our Standard Operating Procedures (SOP). He clearly understands the anchor reset process, required tooling, safety precautions, and operational sequence. He worked efficiently while maintaining a strong focus on safety and compliance.\nProper PPE was worn at all times and in good condition. Pedro maintained situational awareness and demonstrated safe work practices throughout the job.\nOverall, Pedro represented the company professionally on an OXY location. He showed accountability, preparedness, and operational competence. His performance reflects a strong understanding of both safety expectations and technical execution.\n\nEvaluation Summary:\nPedro continues to demonstrate reliability, safety compliance, and technical proficiency in the field. He is a dependable operator who can be trusted to execute work according to both customer and company standards.","location":"BRU- 5304","service_line":"Anchor","report_number":"75912412","yard":"Seminole"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Kevin Dove","type":"Recognition","description":"During the rig up, I noticed that we did not have the pelican hook, which is required on all Chevron jobs. So hand was sent down to grab the hook.","location":"Patterson 289","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75907844","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Roger Gray","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"When running bondco pipe the pipe was running against the guide plate on the fm causing it to were on one side and potentially leading to the collars hitting the segments. Brought up several times that the rig needs to be centered to the cm, driller and the torque turn hands but nothing was done about it. This is costing Butchs money cause we are wearing out guidepltes.","location":" Cactus 404","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75904114","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Michael Salazar","type":"At-Risk Procedure","description":"Only the pre hazard checklist had been completed on the JSA","location":"HP 267","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75901555","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Michael Salazar","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Crew member not wearing his H2S monitor while working on rig floir","location":"HP 267","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75901554","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Marcus Garcia","type":"Recognition","description":"Hand placement on rigging down","location":"Cactus 172","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75899849","yard":""},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Kayla Magana","type":"Recognition","description":"I conducted a field evaluation of Shawn while performing anchor resetting operations. The purpose of this visit was to assess compliance with company safety standards, adherence to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP), and overall field competency.\nThe operator was properly equipped with all required Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including [hard hat, safety glasses, gloves, FR clothing, steel-toe boots, etc.], in accordance with company policy and client site requirements. PPE was worn appropriately throughout the duration of the task.\nDuring the operation, the operator demonstrated working knowledge of anchor resetting procedures, including proper assessment of existing anchor placement, safe removal or repositioning methods, equipment inspection, and reinstallation techniques. The reset was conducted in a controlled and methodical manner while maintaining situational awareness and site safety.\n\nThe operator followed established SOP guidelines and completed the task efficiently while ensuring anchor integrity and job quality standards were maintained.\nOverall, performance met company expectations for safety, compliance, and operational execution.","location":"Mallet 142","service_line":"Anchor","report_number":"75896228","yard":"Levelland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Tanner Evans","type":"Recognition","description":"Bolt for riser snapped in elevators","location":"H&P252","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75895741","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Kayla Magana","type":"Recognition","description":"I conducted a field evaluation of the anchor testing procedures being performed by Daniel Martinez. The purpose of this visit was to observe compliance with company Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and safety requirements.\nThe operator was properly equipped with required Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), including [hard hat, safety glasses, gloves, FR clothing, steel-toe boots, etc.], in accordance with company policy and job site requirements.\nDuring the evaluation, the operator demonstrated familiarity with and adherence to established anchor testing SOPs. Testing procedures were performed in a controlled and methodical manner, with attention to safety, equipment integrity, and accurate data collection.\nOverall, the operator exhibited a clear understanding of proper testing protocols and maintained a safe work environment throughout the operation.","location":"Sundown Unit 94","service_line":"Anchor","report_number":"75894048","yard":"Levelland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Christopher LaCoume","type":"Recognition","description":"Bolts on riser broke on two of the HYC elevators replaced and continued the run safely","location":"252","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75890702","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Bobby Northcutt","type":"Recognition","description":"When rigging up we began to set slips for our bump test when Jacob realized the slip dyes weren't engaging on the pipe correctly, after further examination it looked to be the wrong dyes. We stopped the job ran down and grabbed out back up hand slips. ","location":"Lasso 101","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75884135","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Bobby Northcutt","type":"Recognition","description":"Gio stopped driller from slamming into the pipe with the top drive as the pipe started to float when the driller was coming down","location":"Patterson 278","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75883579","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"John Draper Jr","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Rig hand not wearing ppe ","location":"Icd332","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"75854070","yard":"Midland"},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Nicholas Sanchez","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Third party JES trailer has a blown tire. ","location":"WAR CLUB 3-4 FED COM 822H","service_line":"","report_number":"75905069","yard":""},{"date":"2026-02-25","observer":"Nicholas Sanchez","type":"At-Risk Condition","description":"Hydraulic hose to the rig floor was found to be damaged. ","location":"WAR CLUB 3-4 FED COM 822H","service_line":"","report_number":"75904944","yard":""}]},"near_misses":[],"incidents":[{"date":"2026-02-25","employee":"","type":"Report Only","description":"On 02-25-26, casing crew member was assisting in rigging down the 10\u00be\" CRT on Akita Rig 521. After pushing the CRT over onto the rig floor, the crew member looked upward toward the air hoist to locate the strap for removal. While his eyes were directed upward, he stepped backward and his left knee struck the side of an open, unguarded v-door trough on the rig floor.\n\nThe crew member did not report significant pain at the time of the incident. Upon transport back from the location, he reported increasing soreness and swelling in the left knee. He was taken to Trinity Family Medicine where he was examined and released to full duty with no restrictions. This is a report-only incident.","location":"Akita 521","service_line":"Casing","company":"Butch's Rat Hole & Anchor Service Inc","report_number":"75889689"}],"assessments":{"total":18,"details":[{"date":"2026-02-25","assessor":"Michael Salazar","form_id":381707,"form_name":"CSG - Safety Casing Field Assessment","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"75976770"},{"date":"2026-02-25","assessor":"Michael Salazar","form_id":381707,"form_name":"CSG - Safety Casing Field Assessment","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"75901556"},{"date":"2026-02-25","assessor":"Ruben Lopez","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"75937777"},{"date":"2026-02-25","assessor":"Hurbano Lopez","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"C